        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nMica panels were used to protect the delicate embroidery on this casket. Mica is a mineral that occurs in thin, almost transparent sheets. It is also fragile, so the survival of the mica on this casket is very rare. This casket may also once have had a wooden travelling case. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
